{
  "__doc": "FIX-7, pago de deuda (2026-08-25): los 5 handlers del despachador de edición que estaban en hook-debt.json sin caso propio. Cada caso ejerce el DISPARO REAL vía hook-pre-edit.js / hook-post-edit.js (que es lo registrado en las dos herramientas) y nombra a su handler en el label — el criterio de cobertura del censo. Sus lógicas puras ya tenían suites node; lo que faltaba era el disparo dentro de la herramienta.",
  "hooks": [
    {
      "hook": "hook-pre-edit.js → on-story-gate (portón de carril)",
      "script": "${SKILLS}/skills/tycon-pipeline/scripts/hook-pre-edit.js",
      "event": "PreToolUse",
      "matcher": "Edit|Write",
      "cases": [
        {
          "id": "on-story-gate-deniega-codigo-sin-carril",
          "type": "must-block",
          "setup": ["git init -q -b main .", "mkdir -p .tycon src"],
          "stdin": { "session_id": "bench-sg1", "tool_name": "Write", "tool_input": { "file_path": "${FIXTURE}/src/Nuevo.cs", "content": "class Nuevo {}" } },
          "expect": { "exit": 2, "stderr_re": ["CARRIL|carril"] }
        },
        {
          "id": "on-story-gate-quiet-con-killswitch-del-dev",
          "type": "must-not-block",
          "env": { "TYCON_STORY_GATE": "off" },
          "setup": ["git init -q -b main .", "mkdir -p .tycon src"],
          "stdin": { "session_id": "bench-sg2", "tool_name": "Write", "tool_input": { "file_path": "${FIXTURE}/src/Nuevo.cs", "content": "class Nuevo {}" } },
          "expect": { "exit": 0 }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "hook": "hook-pre-edit.js → on-dod-evidence-guard (la evidencia no se escribe a mano)",
      "script": "${SKILLS}/skills/tycon-pipeline/scripts/hook-pre-edit.js",
      "event": "PreToolUse",
      "matcher": "Edit|Write",
      "cases": [
        {
          "id": "on-dod-evidence-guard-deniega-escribir-la-evidencia-directo",
          "type": "must-block",
          "__doc": "La evidencia de DoD la produce el smoke/checker, no un Write del agente: poder escribirla a mano convierte el gate de cierre en un formulario.",
          "setup": ["git init -q -b main .", "mkdir -p .advisors/dod-runtime .tycon"],
          "stdin": { "session_id": "bench-dg1", "tool_name": "Write", "tool_input": { "file_path": "${FIXTURE}/.advisors/dod-runtime/3.1-20260825.md", "content": "evidencia inventada" } },
          "expect": { "exit": 2 }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "hook": "hook-pre-edit.js → on-atdd-preedit (la prueba antes que el código, preventivo)",
      "script": "${SKILLS}/skills/tycon-pipeline/scripts/hook-pre-edit.js",
      "event": "PreToolUse",
      "matcher": "Edit|Write",
      "cases": [
        {
          "id": "on-atdd-preedit-deniega-el-primer-codigo-sin-tests",
          "type": "must-block",
          "__doc": "Pipeline activo (marker), story que declara ### Tests, step 4 abierto, cero tests tocados → el PRIMER archivo de código se deniega. Las otras dos capas detectan la inversión cuando ya está escrita; ésta la hace imposible.",
          "setup": [
            "git init -q -b main .",
            "mkdir -p .tycon src specs/stories",
            "printf -- '---\\nstory: \"3.1\"\\nepic: \"3\"\\nstatus: in-progress\\n---\\n# Story 3.1\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n1. AC uno\\n\\n### Tests\\n| T | AC | Tipo |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| T1 | 1 | unit |\\n' > specs/stories/3-1.md",
            "node -e \"const fs=require('fs');const d=process.env.SANDBOX_HOME+'/.claude/.tycon-pipeline/active';fs.mkdirSync(d,{recursive:true});fs.writeFileSync(d+'/bench-at1.json',JSON.stringify({sessionId:'bench-at1',storyId:'3.1',repoPath:process.env.FIXTURE,storyPath:process.env.FIXTURE+'/specs/stories/3-1.md',stepsCompleted:[0,1,2,3],fileEvents:[],lastTouch:new Date().toISOString()}))\""
          ],
          "stdin": { "session_id": "bench-at1", "tool_name": "Write", "tool_input": { "file_path": "${FIXTURE}/src/Servicio.cs", "content": "class Servicio {}" } },
          "expect": {
            "exit": 2,
            "stderr_re": ["ATDD"],
            "file_contains": [{ "path": "${SANDBOX_HOME}/.claude/.tycon-pipeline/gates.log", "re": "atdd-preedit" }]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "on-atdd-preedit-quiet-si-ya-hay-un-test-tocado",
          "type": "must-not-block",
          "setup": [
            "git init -q -b main .",
            "mkdir -p .tycon src specs/stories",
            "printf -- '---\\nstory: \"3.1\"\\nepic: \"3\"\\nstatus: in-progress\\n---\\n# Story 3.1\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n1. AC uno\\n\\n### Tests\\n| T | AC | Tipo |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| T1 | 1 | unit |\\n' > specs/stories/3-1.md",
            "node -e \"const fs=require('fs');const d=process.env.SANDBOX_HOME+'/.claude/.tycon-pipeline/active';fs.mkdirSync(d,{recursive:true});fs.writeFileSync(d+'/bench-at2.json',JSON.stringify({sessionId:'bench-at2',storyId:'3.1',repoPath:process.env.FIXTURE,storyPath:process.env.FIXTURE+'/specs/stories/3-1.md',stepsCompleted:[0,1,2,3],fileEvents:[{path:process.env.FIXTURE+'/tests/Servicio.test.ts'}],lastTouch:new Date().toISOString()}))\""
          ],
          "stdin": { "session_id": "bench-at2", "tool_name": "Write", "tool_input": { "file_path": "${FIXTURE}/src/Servicio.cs", "content": "class Servicio {}" } },
          "expect": { "exit": 0 }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "hook": "hook-pre-edit.js → on-write-collision (aviso cross-sesión)",
      "script": "${SKILLS}/skills/tycon-pipeline/scripts/hook-pre-edit.js",
      "event": "PreToolUse",
      "matcher": "Edit|Write",
      "cases": [
        {
          "id": "on-write-collision-avisa-archivo-tocado-por-otra-sesion",
          "type": "must-emit",
          "__doc": "OTRA sesión del pipeline ya tocó este archivo (está en su filesTouched): el aviso tiene que salir — advisory, nunca bloquea. El marker de la sesión propia trae el step 4 cerrado para que el portón ATDD no corte antes.",
          "setup": [
            "git init -q -b main .",
            "mkdir -p .tycon src && printf 'class Foo {}' > src/Foo.cs",
            "node -e \"const fs=require('fs');const d=process.env.SANDBOX_HOME+'/.claude/.tycon-pipeline/active';fs.mkdirSync(d,{recursive:true});fs.writeFileSync(d+'/bench-wc1.json',JSON.stringify({sessionId:'bench-wc1',storyId:'3.1',repoPath:process.env.FIXTURE,stepsCompleted:[0,1,2,3,4],fileEvents:[],filesTouched:[],lastTouch:new Date().toISOString()}));fs.writeFileSync(d+'/bench-wc-otra.json',JSON.stringify({sessionId:'bench-wc-otra',storyId:'3.1',repoPath:process.env.FIXTURE,stepsCompleted:[0,1,2,3,4],filesTouched:[process.env.FIXTURE+'/src/Foo.cs'],fileEvents:[],lastTouch:new Date().toISOString()}))\""
          ],
          "stdin": { "session_id": "bench-wc1", "tool_name": "Edit", "tool_input": { "file_path": "${FIXTURE}/src/Foo.cs", "old_string": "class Foo {}", "new_string": "class Foo { int x; }" } },
          "expect": {
            "exit": 0,
            "stdout_re": ["system-reminder", "Foo\\.cs"]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "hook": "hook-post-edit.js → on-edit (registro de archivos tocados)",
      "script": "${SKILLS}/skills/tycon-pipeline/scripts/hook-post-edit.js",
      "event": "PostToolUse",
      "matcher": "Edit|Write",
      "cases": [
        {
          "id": "on-edit-registra-el-archivo-en-el-marker",
          "type": "must-run",
          "__doc": "El registro que alimenta al gate ATDD y al re-loop: cada Edit/Write con pipeline activo queda anotado en el marker. Sin esto, 'qué archivos tocó esta story' es memoria del modelo.",
          "setup": [
            "git init -q -b main .",
            "mkdir -p .tycon src && printf 'class Foo {}' > src/Foo.cs",
            "node -e \"const fs=require('fs');const d=process.env.SANDBOX_HOME+'/.claude/.tycon-pipeline/active';fs.mkdirSync(d,{recursive:true});fs.writeFileSync(d+'/bench-oe1.json',JSON.stringify({sessionId:'bench-oe1',storyId:'3.1',repoPath:process.env.FIXTURE,stepsCompleted:[0,1,2,3,4],fileEvents:[],filesTouched:[],lastTouch:new Date().toISOString()}))\""
          ],
          "stdin": { "session_id": "bench-oe1", "tool_name": "Edit", "tool_input": { "file_path": "${FIXTURE}/src/Foo.cs", "old_string": "class Foo {}", "new_string": "class Foo { int x; }" } },
          "expect": {
            "file_contains": [{ "path": "${SANDBOX_HOME}/.claude/.tycon-pipeline/active/bench-oe1.json", "re": "Foo\\.cs" }]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "hook": "hook-pre-edit.js → on-frontmatter-write (el estado a mano)",
      "script": "${SKILLS}/skills/tycon-pipeline/scripts/hook-pre-edit.js",
      "event": "PreToolUse",
      "matcher": "Edit|Write",
      "cases": [
        {
          "id": "edit-a-done-frena",
          "type": "must-block",
          "_por_que": "8.109: pasar una historia a done con la herramienta de edición salteaba los controles del cierre.",
          "setup": [
            "git init -q -b main .",
            "mkdir -p .tycon specs",
            "printf -- '---\\nepic: 1\\nstory: \"1.1\"\\ntitle: \"Resta\"\\nstatus: in-progress\\nqa_guide: off\\n---\\n# Story 1.1\\n' > specs/story-1.1-resta.md",
            "node \"$TCG/scripts/controls-bench/conversation-fixture.js\" --who person --text \"cerrala\"",
            "node \"$TCG/scripts/controls-bench/conversation-fixture.js\" --who command"
          ],
          "stdin": {
            "session_id": "bench-escape",
            "tool_name": "Edit",
            "tool_input": {
              "file_path": "${FIXTURE}/specs/story-1.1-resta.md",
              "old_string": "status: in-progress\nqa",
              "new_string": "status: done\nqa"
            },
            "tool_use_id": "bench-tu"
          },
          "expect": {
            "exit": 2,
            "stderr_re": [
              "update-story-status"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "edit-a-done-con-frase-frena",
          "type": "must-block",
          "_por_que": "8.139: «autorizo cambiar el estado» de la persona ya no firma (gemelo del anterior): el cartel nombra la firma de la ventana sobre el archivo.",
          "setup": [
            "git init -q -b main .",
            "mkdir -p .tycon specs",
            "printf -- '---\\nepic: 1\\nstory: \"1.1\"\\ntitle: \"Resta\"\\nstatus: in-progress\\nqa_guide: off\\n---\\n# Story 1.1\\n' > specs/story-1.1-resta.md",
            "node \"$TCG/scripts/controls-bench/conversation-fixture.js\" --who person --text \"autorizo cambiar el estado\"",
            "node \"$TCG/scripts/controls-bench/conversation-fixture.js\" --who command"
          ],
          "stdin": {
            "session_id": "bench-escape",
            "tool_name": "Edit",
            "tool_input": {
              "file_path": "${FIXTURE}/specs/story-1.1-resta.md",
              "old_string": "status: in-progress\nqa",
              "new_string": "status: done\nqa"
            },
            "tool_use_id": "bench-tu"
          },
          "expect": {
            "exit": 2,
            "stderr_re": [
              "sign-file cambiar-el-estado"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
